-- title:
--   Étale p-divisible towers over 𝔽ₚ lift to 𝒪
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring and $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$, $\mathcal O$ carries an algebra structure on $\mathbb Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly the ideal $(p)$, and $\mathcal O$ is adically complete for $(p)$. Let $E_v$ ($v \in \mathbb N$) be commutative rings, each a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $\mathbb Z/p$ that is finite as a $\mathbb Z/p$-module and reduced, and let $s_v \colon E_{v+1} \to E_v$ be bialgebra maps over $\mathbb Z/p$ that are surjective and satisfy $\ker s_v = \mathrm{torsionIdeal}(p^v)$, that is, the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker \varepsilon$ under the algebra endomorphism [`PDivisibleGroup.Hopf.nsmulAlgHom`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L16) given by the $p^v$-fold convolution power of the identity. The assertion is the existence of commutative rings $\tilde E_v$ in the universe of $\mathcal O$, each a cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebra that is finite and free as an $\mathcal O$-module and formally étale over $\mathcal O$, together with bialgebra maps $\tilde s_v \colon \tilde E_{v+1} \to \tilde E_v$ over $\mathcal O$ and bialgebra maps $\theta_v \colon \mathbb Z/p \otimes_{\mathcal O} \tilde E_v \to E_v$ over $\mathbb Z/p$ such that: every $\theta_v$ is bijective; the square commutes, $\theta_v$ precomposed with $\mathrm{id} \otimes \tilde s_v$ equals $\theta_{v+1}$ followed by $s_v$; every $\tilde s_v$ is surjective with $\ker \tilde s_v$ the $p^v$-torsion ideal of $\tilde E_{v+1}$ in the same sense; $\mathrm{rk}_{\mathcal O} \tilde E_v = \dim_{\mathbb Z/p} E_v$; and for every commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $g$ that is adically complete for the ideal generated by $p$ in $g$, and every $v$, composition with the quotient map $g \to g/(p)$ is a bijection from $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\tilde E_v \to g$ onto $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\tilde E_v \to g/(p)$.
--
--   This is the statement that a tower of reduced (étale) finite cocommutative Hopf algebras over $\mathbb F_p$, with the $p$-divisible-group transition and torsion conditions, lifts to a tower of finite free formally étale Hopf algebras over the $p$-adically complete base $\mathcal O$, compatibly with transitions, kernels, ranks and points — the étale part of the classification of $p$-divisible groups along the henselian pair $\mathcal O \to \mathbb F_p$. It is used in the construction of split coordinates and normal forms for Honda systems, via [`Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_splitCoordinates_lawful_normalForm`](thm.html#Deformation.HondaSystem.exists_splitCoordinates_lawful_normalForm).
